<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.renacode.cloudmachine.backup-health</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__CM_AGENT_BIN__</string>
    <string>backup-health</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <!--
    Backup cycle watchdog. The only component that answers the question "is a
    backup STILL being made", rather than "are the devices attached" - those
    two things drift apart silently, and that drift is the most dangerous
    failure here.

    No KeepAlive: this is a one-shot check that exits with code 1 when the
    cycle is broken. KeepAlive would turn every failure into a restart loop.

    Every 30 minutes, with an hourly cycle and a 3 h threshold - often enough
    that a broken cycle does not sit unnoticed for a day, and rarely enough to
    cost nothing. The watchdog reads the local Time Machine preferences file,
    NOT the Google Drive mount: a supervisor that hangs together with what it
    supervises goes silent exactly when it should speak.
  -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__CM_LOG_DIR__/launchd-backup-health.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__CM_LOG_DIR__/launchd-backup-health.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
